LICENSE NOT YET CHOSEN — THIS REPOSITORY IS NOT PUBLISHABLE IN THIS STATE.

No licence has been granted. All rights reserved.

Choosing the licence is a Founder decision and it is the one thing blocking
publication. It is close to irreversible: the version published under a
licence stays available under it forever, and relicensing later needs every
contributor's consent.

The choice interacts directly with the stated business model (an open local
core, with a hosted evidence service as the paid layer):

  Apache-2.0  maximum adoption, explicit patent grant. Anyone, including a
              cloud vendor, may host the paid layer we intend to sell.
  AGPL-3.0    a competitor who hosts it must publish their modifications.
              Protects the hosted business. Some companies forbid AGPL
              dependencies outright, which costs adoption.
  BSL 1.1     source-available, converts to an open licence after a set term,
              forbids competing hosted services in the meantime. Not OSI-
              approved, so it cannot be called open source.

Replace this file with the chosen licence text before making the repository
public.
